; [1561] 
; [1562] { ================================================================
; [1563]   31: Parameter-indexed stores        (Part 26 regression)
; [1564] 
; [1565]   `A[v] := x' where v is a PARAMETER stored nothing -- or rather, it
; [1566]   stored into v's own frame slot. EmitAddress set DestIsXY2 on the first
; [1567]   frame access in the LHS, which for a subscripted destination is the
; [1568]   INDEX, so EmitStore's [XY2+#N] fast path fired with the index's offset.
; [1569]   The element address was computed correctly and discarded.
; [1570] 
; [1571]   Nothing in the suite caught it: every array store here indexes with a
; [1572]   global or a var-section local, both of which are page-addressed and take
; [1573]   the generic indirect path. Seven of nine shapes were broken and the
; [1574]   whole suite still passed.
; [1575] 
; [1576]   The failure was silent in the worst way -- reads through the same
; [1577]   parameter index were correct, so an array written through a setter kept
; [1578]   returning its old contents with no fault and no wrong value.
; [1579] 
; [1580]   `store did not hit v' below is the direct assertion: before the fix, v
; [1581]   came back holding the value that should have gone into the array.
; [1582]   ================================================================ }
